#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tables"
msgstr "Tablèus"

#. Tag: primary
#: table.docbook:12 table.docbook:30 table.docbook:92 table.docbook:100
#: table.docbook:120 table.docbook:157 table.docbook:190 table.docbook:222
#: table.docbook:257 table.docbook:284 table.docbook:335 table.docbook:359
#: table.docbook:369 table.docbook:386 table.docbook:399 table.docbook:445
#: table.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "tables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "using"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the built in ability to generate tables for the display of data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These tables can consist of up to 128 rows and 128 columns, with text "
"centered or justified differently in different cells. Text flows easily "
"around in the table and cells are resized (if specified by the user) "
"automatically to fit comfortably around the data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tables in &kword; are for the display of data only. No calculations can be "
"performed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remember, if you need the functions of a spreadsheet, you can <link linkend="
"\"kparts\">embed a &kspread; Table</link> in your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the document will cover the formatting of tables "
"<emphasis>created in &kword;</emphasis> only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a new Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "adding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can create a table in &kword; in one of three ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Table...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F5</"
"keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"part-"
"kspread.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the "
"toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will open a dialog box. The dialog box has two tabs: "
"<guilabel>Geometry</guilabel> and <guilabel>Templates</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "This dialog box is divided into two halves."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The right half of the dialog box provides you a quick visual guide to how "
"many rows and columns will be created in the table. This is useful for "
"laying out your table. You cannot edit your table layout here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "The left half of the dialog box consists of two combo boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spin box labeled <guilabel>Number of rows:</guilabel>, allows you to "
"specify from 1 to 128 rows in the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spin box labeled <guilabel>Number of columns:</guilabel>, allows you to "
"specify from 1 to 128 columns in the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While adjusting either of these two options, the preview box adjusts to your "
"new settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on the tab labeled <guilabel>Templates</guilabel>, you can use "
"predefined table looks to format the look of your table. For more "
"information see the section on <link linkend=\"table-templates\">Using "
"formatting templates</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to insert the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to cancel this action and return to "
"editing your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving between cells in a table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "navigating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can navigate between cells of the table by using the mouse (simply click "
"in the cell you want to edit), or by using the keyboard (use the arrow keys "
"to move up, down, left or right one cell at a time)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:100 table.docbook:585
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "To delete a table in &kword;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse pointer over the frame of any cell of the table you want to "
"delete and click once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be sure you have selected the correct table before continuing. &kword; will "
"not ask for confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Delete Table</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "The table will be immediately deleted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Row in Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "inserting a row"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can insert a row into any place in a table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert a row into a table, place the mouse pointer over the border of any "
"cell of the table you want to add a row to. Using your mouse, select either "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Row</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Insert Row...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar or "
"click <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"rowin.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:134 table.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will bring up a dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spin box labeled <guilabel>Row:</guilabel>, allows you to select any row "
"within the table. This number selection box limits you to the rows currently "
"in the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the row you want to use as a reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:147 table.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now select either <guilabel>Before</guilabel> or <guilabel>After</guilabel> "
"as is appropriate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to add the row or click <guibutton>Cancel</"
"guibutton> to not add any rows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Column in Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "inserting a column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert a column into a table, place the mouse pointer over the border of "
"any cell of the table you want to add a column to. Select either "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Insert Column...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar or "
"click <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"colin.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number selection box labeled <guilabel>Column:</guilabel>, allows you to "
"select any column within the table. This number selection box limits you to "
"the columns currently in the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the column you want to use as a reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to add the column or click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to not add any columns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete Row in Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting a row"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "To delete a row from a table:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click once with the &LMB; in any cell in the row you want to delete Then:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Row</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Delete Selected Rows...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or click <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"rowout.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box confirming that your have selected the "
"correct row(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make sure you have selected the correct row(s) before continuing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; will delete any data contained within the selected rows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> to delete the row, or click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to not delete any rows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete Column in Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting a column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "To delete a column from a table:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click once with the &LMB; in any cell in the column you want to delete Then:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Delete Selected Columns...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or click <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"colout.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box confirming that your have selected the "
"correct column(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make sure you have selected the correct column(s) before continuing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; will delete any data contained within these columns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> to delete the column(s), or click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to not delete any columns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change column width"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "change column width"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a table is created, all columns are equal in width. You can change the "
"width of individual columns by using <link linkend=\"table-resize-column-"
"mouse\">the mouse</link> or <link linkend=\"table-resize-column-dialog\">the "
"keyboard</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First select any cell in the column you want to change, by holding down the "
"&Ctrl; key and clicking once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cell is now surrounded by 8 colored boxes. Place the mouse over the box "
"in the middle of the right vertical border of the cell. The mouse pointer "
"changes to a double-headed arrow. Click on the box and drag the right edge "
"of the cell to the desired width. When you release the &LMB;, the entire "
"column will assume the width of this cell."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the dialog box"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, select any cell in the column you want to change, by holding down the "
"&Ctrl; key and clicking once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select any cell in the table to change column widths. By selecting a "
"cell in the column you want to change the dialog box will default to the "
"correct column automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Resize Column...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A dialog box will appear. In the spin box labeled <guilabel>Column:</"
"guilabel>, you can chose a different column to set. In the spin box labeled "
"<guilabel>Width:</guilabel>, enter the desired width of the column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to change the width, or click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to leave the column width unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Join Cells in Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "join cells"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A table is traditionally made of a grid of rows and columns, with equal "
"sized cells throughout the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes you would like to spread text out over several cells in a table. "
"This is especially common with titles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; allows you to do this by <emphasis>Joining</emphasis> two (or more) "
"adjacent cells of a table together."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is an example of three cells joined together in the middle of a table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can join cells vertically, as well as horizontally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To join several cells you must first select the cells. To select the cells, "
"hold down the &Ctrl; key and click once with the &LMB; in a cell. Click on "
"the next cell with the &LMB;. Continue this until you have selected all the "
"cells you want to join together."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a number of cells in a row that you want to select, you can "
"select them in two quick steps:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "First hold down the &Ctrl; key and click on one of the end cells."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now hold down the &Shift; key and click on the cell at the other end of the "
"row or column you want to join."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid "All cells between these two cells will be selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected all the cells you want to join, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Cell</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Join "
"Cells</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "The cells will now be joined."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any text in the left most frame will now be located in the joined frame. Any "
"text from any other frames will be deleted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Split Cells in Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "split cells"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to combining two or more cells into a single cell, it is easy to "
"split one cell into many cells."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you decide that you do not want the previously joined cells to be joined "
"any longer, you can <quote>split</quote> them back into individual cells "
"again. You can also split cells within a column or row. They do not need to "
"have been previously joined."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To split a cell, select the cell you want to split by holding the &Ctrl; "
"button down and clicking on it with the &LMB;. Select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Cell</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Split "
"Cell...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a small dialog box which allows you to set the number of "
"rows and the number of columns you want to split this cell into."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have set the correct number of rows and columns in the spin boxes, "
"click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to split the cells. Click <guibutton>Cancel</"
"guibutton> to abort."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ungroup a Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "ungrouping"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select a cell in a table and then choose <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Ungroup Table</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar, &kword; will convert each cell in your table into an individual "
"frame. You can then move these frames around independently on the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Protecting a cell in a table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "protecting cells"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can protect any or all cells in a table from accidental modification or "
"deletion."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simply select the cell(s) you want to protect, then:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Cell</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Protect Cells</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar or hold down the &Ctrl; button, click in the cell once with the "
"&RMB; and select <menuchoice> <guimenuitem>Cell</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Protect Cells</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"popup menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "You will not be able to change the contents or formatting of that cell."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To disable the protection, simply repeat the steps above, and the cells will "
"no longer be protected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formating a Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "formating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are many aspects of a table that can be formatted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information of formatting text with a table see <link linkend=\"change-"
"font\">Format characters</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information on formatting borders between frames in individual cells, "
"see <link linkend=\"para-borders\">Borders</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information on formatting background color of individual cells, see "
"<link linkend=\"format-frame-background\">Frame background</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information on changing the width of columns, see <link linkend=\"table-"
"resize-column\">Resizing Columns</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; also provides the user with a set of tools to help speed up the "
"formatting of tables."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "Altering the number of rows and columns in a table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "changing geometry"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Previously in the manual, we have discussed how to individually add or "
"delete rows and/or columns. &kword; also provides the user the ability to "
"make major changes to the number of rows and columns in a table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Properties...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this dialog to change the number of rows in your table by using "
"the spin box labeled <guilabel>Number of rows:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you reduce the number of rows using this dialog box, &kword; will delete "
"the bottom row(s) <emphasis>including the data within the rows</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be sure you do not have any data in these rows that you need to preserve."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this dialog to change the number of columns in your table by "
"using the spin box labeled <guilabel>Number of columns:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you reduce the number of columns using this dialog box, &kword; will "
"delete the right most column(s) <emphasis>including the data within the "
"columns</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be sure you do not have any data in these columns that you need to preserve."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:424 table.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Placing a mark in the check box labeled <guilabel>Reapply template to table</"
"guilabel>, will cause &kword; to re-apply the template to the table "
"<emphasis>after adding or deleting the specified number of rows and/or "
"columns</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:426 table.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to make changes permenant, or click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to abort all changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting an entire column for formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select an entire column for formatting, move the mouse pointer to the "
"white space directly <emphasis>above</emphasis> the desired column. The "
"mouse pointer will turn from an arrow to a hand. If you click with the "
"&LMB;, the entire column will be selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting an entire row for formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select an entire row for formatting, move the mouse pointer to the white "
"space directly <emphasis>to the left</emphasis> of the desired row. The "
"mouse pointer will turn from an arrow to a hand. If you click with the "
"&LMB;, the entire row will be selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using table templates to format an entire table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has templates for many commonly used table formatting options. Table "
"templates provide the same formatting functionality for tables that document "
"templates provide you for formating your documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Properties...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog will appear. Click on "
"the tab labeled <guilabel>Templates</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid "Along the left of the dialog box, is a list of table templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right is a preview box that gives an example of what a table template "
"will look like when applied to your table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid "Below the preview box, are 5 check boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: table.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "First row"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "This check box will toggle formatting of all cells in the top row."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: table.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid "Last row"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid "This check box will toggle formatting of all cells in the bottom row."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: table.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Body"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This check box will toggle formatting of all cells in the body. The body of "
"the table is any cells which are not formatted by any of the other four "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: table.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "First column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid "This check box will toggle formatting of all cells in the left column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: table.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "Last column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "This check box will toggle formatting of all cells in the right column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using table styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: table.docbook:509 table.docbook:516 table.docbook:529 table.docbook:561
#: table.docbook:585 table.docbook:605 table.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid "table styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Table styles are a rapid way for you to format individual cells of your "
"table to common formats. You can add or remove table styles, and change "
"predefined table styles to suit your needs. A table style consists of a "
"frame style and a text style which are grouped together and named."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting a cell with a table styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting a cell with"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid "To format a cell using a predefined table style simply:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the cell(s) by holding down &Ctrl; and clicking within the cell with "
"the &LMB;. You can also <link linkend=\"table-format-selcol\">select "
"columns</link> and <link linkend=\"table-format-selrow\">rows</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Tablestyle</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice> from the menubar. A submenu will appear, listing "
"all the currently defined table styles. Select the name of the table style "
"you want and all selected cells will automatically be formatting using the "
"options of that table style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing a table style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid "editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the options of a table style, you will use the Table Style Manager."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table Style "
"Manager...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All of the currently defined table styles are listed in the listbox on the "
"left. The currently selected table style is highlighted, and the name of the "
"currently selected table style is listed in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Name</guilabel>. (In this example, the currently selected table "
"style is <emphasis>Header 1</emphasis>.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the name of the table style you want to change by clicking on the "
"name of the table style in the listbox on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the section labeled <guilabel>Adjust</guilabel> is a combo box labeled "
"<guilabel>Framestyle</guilabel> which is used to select the desired frame "
"style. If you want to add or alter a frame style, click the "
"<guilabel>Change...</guilabel> button, and you will be taken to the <link "
"linkend=\"framestyle-edit\">Framestylist</link> to make those changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below that, is a combo box labeled <guilabel>Textstyle:</guilabel> which is "
"used to select the desired text style for this table style. If you want to "
"add or alter a text style, click on the <guilabel>Change...</guilabel> "
"button, and you will be taken directly to the <link linkend=\"style-add-"
"dialog\">Stylelist</link> to make those changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once all changes have been made, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save "
"your changes. All of the affected table styles will be changed to reflect "
"the new options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a new table style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid "creating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new table style, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Table Style Manager...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select a table style from the list at the left which most closely matches "
"your new desired table style. The selected table style will be used as a "
"template for the new table style. Select the table style by clicking once "
"with the &LMB; in the list on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button. &kword; will generate a new "
"table style, which is a copy of the previously selected table style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose a name for your new table style, and type it in the text box labeled "
"<guilabel>Name</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now change your table style options to customize your newly created "
"table style. For details, see <link linkend=\"tablestyle-edit\">Editing a "
"table style</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a table style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete table style, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Table</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Table Style Manager...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the table style you want to delete by clicking once with the &LMB; on "
"the name of the table style you want to delete."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will not allow you to delete the <emphasis>Plain</emphasis> table "
"style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the order of the table style in the list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid "reordering"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the order that the table style are listed, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table Style Manager...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The order the table styles are listed in the menu is determined by the order "
"of the table styles in the list on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the table style you want to move from the list at the left by "
"clicking once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click on the <guiicon>Up Arrow</guiicon> and <guiicon>Down Arrow</"
"guiicon> located at the bottom of the list of table styles. This will move "
"theselected table style up or down in the list of table styles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are satisfied with the order of the list, select <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: table.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid "Importing a table style from another &kword; file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: table.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid "importing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To import a table style from another &kword; file, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table Style Manager...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the button labeled <guibutton>Import From File</guibutton>. You can "
"select the &kword; file using the <link linkend=\"file-dialog\">file "
"selection dialog</link>. Choose your file, and click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A new dialog box will appear listing all available table styles for "
"importing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &kword; encounters a duplicate table style name in the selected file, it "
"will append a number to the end of the table style name to identify the "
"imported style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:644
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example, if you import the <emphasis>Plain</emphasis> table style from "
"another &kword; file, &kword; will change the name to <emphasis>Plain-1</"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <emphasis>all</emphasis> the table styles you want to import. Then "
"click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: table.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The table styles will now appear at the bottom of your list of table styles. "
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to save the table styles in the new document."
msgstr ""
